---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy information for the static Red River Gorge Hiker website and external Fine Art America purchases."
>
  <div class="page prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy information</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <section>
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>RedRiverGorgeHiker.com is designed as a simple static photography website. It does not create visitor accounts, operate a direct shopping cart, or directly collect payment-card information.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Information you choose to provide</h2>
      <p>If you email Ryan, the message may contain your name, email address, organization, request details, and any other information you choose to provide. That information is used to read and respond to the message, maintain relevant business records, address a permission or partnership request, or correct a website issue.</p>
      <p>Do not send payment-card numbers, passwords, government identification numbers, medical information, or other unnecessary sensitive information by email.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Purchase information</h2>
      <p>Online purchases are completed on Fine Art America rather than RedRiverGorgeHiker.com. Fine Art America controls the customer account, checkout, payment, order, shipping, return, and transaction information submitted through its service. Review Fine Art America’s current privacy policy and terms before completing a purchase.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Automatic technical information</h2>
      <p>The first-edition website is intended to launch without advertising pixels or unnecessary third-party tracking scripts. The website host, domain provider, browser, network, and ordinary internet infrastructure may still process technical information needed to deliver and secure the site, such as an IP address, request time, requested page, browser information, and error or security logs.</p>
      <p>If privacy-respecting analytics are added later, this policy must be updated before or when the analytics are activated. The updated policy should identify the provider, information collected, purpose, retention, and available visitor choices.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>The first-edition site is not intended to set marketing or advertising cookies. Essential browser or hosting behavior may change if a future feature is added. This policy must be reviewed before any feature that stores visitor preferences, identifiers, form data, or analytics information is activated.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>Links to Fine Art America or another external service take visitors away from RedRiverGorgeHiker.com. The external service’s privacy and security practices apply after the visitor enters that service.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>The website is not directed to children as an online service and does not intentionally request personal information from children. A child should not send personal information through email without the involvement of a parent or guardian.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>Business email and permission correspondence may be retained when reasonably useful for responding to the request, documenting permission, maintaining business records, resolving a dispute, or meeting legal and accounting needs. Information that is no longer reasonably needed should not be retained merely because it was received.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>Personal information received directly by email is not sold to advertisers. It may be shared when reasonably necessary with a service provider supporting the request, with a professional adviser, to protect rights or security, to comply with law or legal process, or when the sender asks or authorizes the sharing.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>Reasonable care is used with business records and accounts, but no email system, website, network, or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure. Visitors should limit submitted information to what is reasonably necessary for the request.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Privacy questions</h2>
      <p>Questions or correction requests may be sent to <a href="mailto:Ryan@RedRiverGorgeHiker.com">Ryan@RedRiverGorgeHiker.com</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Policy changes</h2>
      <p>This privacy page may be revised when website features, service providers, or business practices change. The current version published on RedRiverGorgeHiker.com controls.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
